I decided to try a tourist character. They are actually much easier
than I expected, or am I getting more adept. It seems I took several
tourist instances past Sokoban and the mines before YASDing. Many
YASDs could be prevented just by remembering to use the damn camera.

Anyway, this latest instance as with all my characters comes from a
clan where coming up with a new name is too much effort. All my
characters are called Mark. Strangely on the final restart of the
game, typed mark (in lower case) and that's how it was posted on the
top 10. Bug? This was using version 3.4.0.

With plenty of food, tourist can afford to go slow. I let my pet
(dog/cat?) get all the grid bugs/rats/geckos/etc. The medium to large
stuff I handle from a distance with my trustee +2 darts until such a
time as I get some good daggers to quiver. For this run, I also picked
up a short sword which I enhanced to expert (hey, it worked didn't it)
until I had a better melee weapon (Vorpee).

In the mines I found a bag of holding (and many more during the
adventure). At one point I was well set up with speed
boots/mitril/gloves/[oProtection/[oR for about -20 AC. But of course I
stepped on a *&(^(*%^ polytrap and turned into something. The problem
was I had a =oRegen that I could not remove. I was worried that I
would not be able to end this polymorphed version of myself by
throwing weapons up to fall on my head, but eventually the damage was
sufficient. So off I went looking for replacement armour and cape.

There were many 7 altars/temples through the dungeon. I bought
protection and sacked from many locations. My 1st gift was Vorpee,
which I kept throughout the rest of the game as a role playing
decision. With an improved =Increase Damage (+5) thanks to the PYEC, I
was lethal.

Eventually, I received a wish (+3 GDSM) from an expensive lamp I
purchased from the minetown. With a =Regen, the Quest was a cakewalk.
At this point I had encountered a few Ls and mindflayers without a big
deal, so I decided to go genocideless for the first time. However, I
had no qualms about wishing and polypiling (without much effort or
success). 

The castle was breached with effort and caution, but few scary
moments. I meant to use a /oS (to lazy to pull it out of the BoH) to
kill the drawbridge but instead I used a wand of opening. So all the
meanies including Ls and a mind flayer poured out. I handled the mob
by retreating to the corridor. Wishes went to: helm of brilliance
(already had telepathy from the PYEC), gauntlets of dexterity (I
wanted to do some spell casting), 2 cursed scrolls of genocide (nurse
dancing pumped up my hps by more than 150), some magic markers. I
never found a scroll of charging, but with the tourist's quest
artifact it's redundant (so that's one saved wish).

Hell was uninteresting to the point of boredom. I even took down
Asmodeus and the other one just for fun. Whack, Whack Jubilex is dead.
Whack, Whack Orcus is dead. Dagger, dagger, dagger Vlad melts away.

Rodney gave up The Book to my /oD. I had loads of fun wading through
the sea of insects summoned in the sanctum. I had some friends (grey
dragon, purple worm, Troll) help me thin out the numbers. A demi-L was
very annoying but in no way threatening. I had prepared several B?oRC.
Rodney double troubled the high priest with The Amulet. They all
eventually went down to my /oD.

During the tedious climb to the surface, I had an another encounter
with the cowardly Rodney. He ran away and I think I let him be to
continue my climb. 

